       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions, and it's the dose I'd guess you meant.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for pain or fever.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and add the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it."
