     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose, and no indication I know of supports it. I'd be putting a dose in the system that could seriously harm the patient, with GI hemorrhage and acute kidney injury the main risks. The extra drug wouldn't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because ibuprofen's effect plateaus well below that dose.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose)\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day, which may be what the \"1600\" was meant to be)\n\nIf the goal is stronger symptom control by this afternoon, I can also enter an adjunct such as scheduled acetaminophen, up to 1 g every 6\u20138 hours. If you have a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, you can discuss it with pharmacy, and I can enter the order once there's a documented indication and pharmacy agrees.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
